kosha shelf

  -- a horizontal surface attached to a wall, at some height above the floor.
  -- an elevated floor for objects. gravity still acts downward.
  -- object on shelf: normal force from shelf = weight of object.
  -- if the object slides off the shelf → falls under gravity → collision with floor.
  -- potential energy = mgh where h is the shelf height above floor.
  -- when the object falls: PE converts to KE → velocity at floor = √(2gh).

